{
  "an5.168:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.168 ",
  "an5.168:0.2": "17. Resentment ",
  "an5.168:0.3": "Ethics ",
  "an5.168:1.1": "There Venerable Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an5.168:1.2": "“Reverends, an unethical person, who lacks ethics, has destroyed a vital condition for right immersion. ",
  "an5.168:1.3": "When there is no right immersion, one who lacks right immersion has destroyed a vital condition for true knowledge and vision. ",
  "an5.168:1.4": "When there is no true knowledge and vision, one who lacks true knowledge and vision has destroyed a vital condition for disillusionment and dispassion. ",
  "an5.168:1.5": "When there is no disillusionment and dispassion, one who lacks disillusionment and dispassion has destroyed a vital condition for knowledge and vision of freedom. ",
  "an5.168:1.6": "Suppose there was a tree that lacked branches and foliage. ",
  "an5.168:1.7": "Its shoots, bark, softwood, and heartwood would not grow to fullness. ",
  "an5.168:1.8": "In the same way, an unethical person, who lacks ethics, has destroyed a vital condition for right immersion. ",
  "an5.168:1.9": "When there is no right immersion, one who lacks right immersion has destroyed a vital condition for true knowledge and vision. ",
  "an5.168:1.10": "When there is no true knowledge and vision, one who lacks true knowledge and vision has destroyed a vital condition for disillusionment and dispassion. ",
  "an5.168:1.11": "When there is no disillusionment and dispassion, one who lacks disillusionm